@node [stream]
@section [stream]
@anchor{#stream}
Local AF_UNIX subscription stream --- the same 276-byte binary packets
as @code{[highrate]}, but over a @code{SOCK_STREAM} socket. Same-host
consumers get a loss-free stream and subscribe by connecting (up to 8 at
once). Slow consumers get dropped packets (visible as @code{imu_seq}
gaps), never a stalled daemon. An optional TCP listener serves the same
framed packets to remote consumers --- a laptop's @code{imud-mon}/Python
client or a bridge on another machine (@code{imud_connect_tcp} /
@code{ImudClient.connect_tcp}). @strong{[restart]}: @code{enabled},
@code{socket}, @code{tcp_enabled}, @code{tcp_bind_addr},
@code{tcp_port}. @strong{[hot]}: @code{rate_hz}.

@multitable @columnfractions 0.21 0.09 0.34 0.37 
@headitem 
Key
 @tab Type
 @tab Default
 @tab Description
@item 
@code{enabled}
 @tab bool
 @tab @code{true}
 @tab Enable the subscription stream --- the one output a stock daemon
provides (the bridges and libimud consumers read it).
@item 
@code{socket}
 @tab string
 @tab @code{"/run/imud/imud-stream.sock"}
 @tab Listen path (mode 0660, owner @code{imud:imud} --- a consumer
needs @code{adduser <user> imud}).
@item 
@code{rate_hz}
 @tab int
 @tab @code{100}
 @tab Per-subscriber packet rate in Hz (AF_UNIX and TCP); must be
greater than zero. Hot-reloadable.
@item 
@code{tcp_enabled}
 @tab bool
 @tab @code{false}
 @tab TCP listener carrying the same framed packets over the network ---
lossless like the AF_UNIX socket.
@item 
@code{tcp_bind_addr}
