Reader threads never block on storage --- a stalled SD card drops
capture records (counted; @code{imud-status} shows a @code{Capture:}
line), never sensor samples. A power cut leaves a valid file with a
truncated tail.

@node Bridge sections their own files
@section Bridge sections (their own files)
@anchor{#bridge-sections-their-own-files}
The optional bridge daemons --- @code{imud-signalk}, @code{imud-mqtt},
@code{imud-influxdb}, @code{imud-mavlink}, @code{imud-prometheus} ---
each read their @strong{own} config file
(@code{/etc/imud/imud-<name>.conf}, an @code{[imud-<name>]} section),
never @code{imud.conf}. Their config keys are documented in each
bridge's own manual and @code{imud-<name>.conf(5)}; see
