@node [position]
@section [position]
@anchor{#position}
Magnetic declination and true heading. @strong{[hot]:}
@code{declination_deg}, @code{lat_deg}, @code{lon_deg}, @code{wmm_file}
--- declination and the WMM field reference are recomputed on SIGHUP (a
live position source owns declination while gpsd/Signal K is enabled).
@strong{[restart]:} the @code{gpsd_*} / @code{signalk_*} source keys and
@code{fix_max_age_h}.

When declination is known, imud adds @code{$HCHDT} to the NMEA stream
and sets @code{FLAG_DECLINATION_VALID} (with the @code{declination_deg}
field) in the binary packet. A known position also lets the filter set
its magnetic reference (field strength and dip) analytically from the
World Magnetic Model, which improves heading accuracy, and --- with live
GPS --- enables a speed-aided centripetal correction that keeps the
horizon level through sustained turns.

@strong{Declination modes (highest priority wins):}

@enumerate 
@item
@strong{WMM auto-compute} --- set @code{lat_deg} and @code{lon_deg}
(both non-zero). imud loads the WMM2025 coefficient file at startup and
on SIGHUP, computes the local declination, and applies it immediately.
Accurate to ±0.5° for a fixed installation.
@item
@strong{Static override} --- set @code{declination_deg} only (leave
@code{lat_deg} and @code{lon_deg} at @code{0.0}). Look up your value at
@url{https://www.ngdc.noaa.gov/geomag/calculators/magcalc.shtml}. East
declination is positive; west is negative.
@item
@strong{Disabled} (default) --- all three at zero → no true-heading
output.
@end enumerate

@strong{Static position and WMM}

@multitable @columnfractions 0.23 0.09 0.15 0.53 
@headitem 
Key
 @tab Type
 @tab Default
 @tab Description
@item 
@code{declination_deg}
 @tab float
 @tab @code{0.0}
 @tab Static declination in degrees. East positive (+), west negative
(−). Ignored when @code{lat_deg} and @code{lon_deg} are both non-zero.
@item 
@code{lat_deg}
 @tab double
 @tab @code{0.0}
 @tab Geodetic latitude in decimal degrees (+N / −S). Set with
@code{lon_deg} to enable WMM auto-compute.
@item 
@code{lon_deg}
 @tab double
 @tab @code{0.0}
 @tab Geodetic longitude in decimal degrees (+E / −W). Set with
@code{lat_deg} to enable WMM auto-compute.
@item 
@code{wmm_file}
 @tab string
 @tab @code{""} (auto)
 @tab Path to the WMM coefficient file. Empty = auto-resolve:
@code{/etc/imud/WMM.COF} if present (operator override), else
@code{/usr/share/imud/WMM.COF} (@code{imud-wmm-data} package /
@code{make install-wmm-data}). Bundled model WMM2025, valid
2025.0--2030.0.
@end multitable

@strong{Live position sources}

Enable one or both to receive GPS-driven WMM updates as the vessel
moves. WMM is recomputed when position changes by ≥ 0.05° (≈ 5 km).
Priority: @strong{gpsd} (live stream) > @strong{SignalK} (polled
fallback) > @strong{static lat/lon} > @strong{static declination}.

@emph{gpsd:}

@multitable @columnfractions 0.19 0.09 0.18 0.54 
@headitem 
Key
 @tab Type
 @tab Default
 @tab Description
@item 
@code{gpsd_enabled}
 @tab bool
 @tab @code{false}
 @tab Connect to gpsd for live position (and speed). gpsd must be
running with a working GPS source.
@item 
@code{gpsd_host}
 @tab string
 @tab @code{"localhost"}
 @tab Hostname or IP of the gpsd instance.
@item 
