@bigskip@hrule@bigskip
@end iftex
@ifnottex
------------------------------------------------------------------------
@end ifnottex

@node 9 Consumer libraries
@chapter 9. Consumer libraries
@anchor{#9-consumer-libraries}
The @code{lib/} directory has ready-to-use clients for the binary
stream, and a microcontroller client lives in its own repository:

@itemize
@item
@strong{C} --- @strong{libimud} (@code{#include <imud.h>}, link
@code{-limud}, @code{pkg-config libimud}): the ABI-stable shared library
--- applications keep working across imud upgrades without recompiling.
Connects to the local socket (@code{imud_connect_stream}), the UDP
stream (@code{imud_connect_udp}), or a remote daemon's @code{[stream]}
TCP listener (@code{imud_connect_tcp}, 1.6). See @code{man 3 libimud}.
@item
@strong{Python} --- @code{lib/imud_client.py}: Python 3.8+, standard
library only. Receives UDP or connects to the TCP stream listener
(@code{ImudClient.connect_tcp(host, port)}). The
@code{ImudPacket.true_heading_deg} property returns @code{None} when
declination is unavailable.
@item
@strong{Arduino/ESP32} ---
@uref{https://github.com/richcreations/imud-arduino,imud-arduino}
(library name @code{ImudClient}), maintained in its own repository.
Header-only Arduino library (Arduino IDE and PlatformIO) that receives
the stream over the @code{[stream]} TCP listener (port 10112) or
high-rate UDP (port 10111, multicast included) through any Arduino
@code{Client}/@code{UDP} transport. Wire-pinned: it is updated alongside
wire revisions.
@item
@strong{C single-header} --- @code{lib/imud_client.h} is
@strong{deprecated}: it pins the wire version (recompile per revision).
Kept in the source tree for existing vendored copies and imud's own
wire-pinned internals; no longer installed by @code{make install}.
@end itemize

All validate CRC32 and support multicast. @code{make install} installs
libimud (library, header, pkg-config) and the Python module to
@code{/usr/local/share/imud}. See @code{man 3 libimud} for the API,
@code{imud_data_t} fields and the ABI contract; the @code{libimud}
package ships fuller usage examples under
@code{/usr/share/doc/libimud/}.

@iftex
@bigskip@hrule@bigskip
@end iftex
@ifnottex
------------------------------------------------------------------------
@end ifnottex

@node 9a Bridges
@chapter 9a. Bridges
@anchor{#9a-bridges}
imud has optional @strong{bridge daemons} that republish its stream into
other ecosystems. Each is a @strong{separate, optional package} with its
own config file, systemd service, man pages, and documentation (README +
manual + spec) --- installed under @code{/usr/share/doc/imud-<name>/},
and in this tree under @code{docs/imud-<name>/}:

@multitable @columnfractions 0.23 0.34 0.43 
@headitem 
Bridge
 @tab Output
 @tab Docs
@item 
@code{imud-signalk}
 @tab Signal K delta JSON over UDP / TCP
 @tab @code{docs/imud-signalk/}, @code{imud-signalk(8)}
@item 
@code{imud-mqtt}
 @tab MQTT topics + Home Assistant discovery
 @tab @code{docs/imud-mqtt/}, @code{imud-mqtt(8)}
@item 
@code{imud-influxdb}
 @tab InfluxDB line protocol (UDP / HTTP)
 @tab @code{docs/imud-influxdb/}, @code{imud-influxdb(8)}
@item 
@code{imud-mavlink}
 @tab MAVLink v1/v2 (UDP / serial / TCP)
 @tab @code{docs/imud-mavlink/}, @code{imud-mavlink(8)}
@item 
@code{imud-prometheus}
 @tab Prometheus @code{/metrics} HTTP exporter
 @tab @code{docs/imud-prometheus/}, @code{imud-prometheus(8)}
@end multitable

All read imud's local stream, so they require
@code{[stream] enabled = true} in @code{imud.conf}. Build them with
@code{make bridges} and install each with
@code{sudo make install-<name>}. See each bridge's @strong{README} for a
quick overview, its @strong{manual} for configuration and setup, and its
@strong{spec} for the exact output format.

Each bridge separates the daemon-level @code{enabled} from its
per-output enables. A stock installed config ships the daemon
@code{enabled = true} but @strong{every output off} (@code{udp_enabled}
/ @code{tcp_enabled} for signalk, @code{udp_enabled} /
@code{http_enabled} for influxdb, @code{broker_enabled} for mqtt,
@code{http_enabled} for prometheus, @code{udp_enabled} /
@code{serial_enabled} / @code{tcp_enabled} for mavlink) --- so the
service starts and stays healthy under systemd while emitting nothing
until you turn on the output(s) you want. Setting the daemon
@code{enabled = false} makes it exit cleanly (systemd stops it; no
restart loop). (imud-influxdb's old @code{transport = "udp"|"http"} key
is deprecated but still honored, mapped to the matching output enable
with a warning.)

